/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# pixi manages the Python environment; the materialised env is not source.
/.pixi
__pycache__/

# Local editor / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Nix / devenv / direnv
/result
/result-*
.direnv/
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
# Personal, uncommitted devenv overrides - the escape hatch that stops people
# editing devenv.nix to make their own machine work.
devenv.local.nix

# prek / pre-commit hook caches
.pre-commit-cache/
.prek-cache/

# Mirror/proxy values for a network without direct egress. Deliberately NOT committed:
# the repo carries public defaults, the site-specific routing stays out of it.
.env

# Ponytail activation flag: local, per-developer.
.ponytail-active

# The rendered site. `mkdocs build` writes it; the markdown in docs/ is the source.
/site

# The CRAP delta's working files: this commit's baseline lifted out of the Nix store, the base
# commit's downloaded artifact, and the rendered pull-request comment. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
# writes all three into the workspace and `just crap-delta` can too; none of them is source, and
# the committed one would rot the moment anything changed.
/crap-baseline.json
/crap-base/
/crap-delta.md

# Scratch written by agent tooling into the working tree. Neither is source, and neither should
# ever reach a commit here - `.playwright-mcp/` holds verbatim dumps of whatever pages a browser
# tool visited, which in THIS repository is a disclosure question rather than a tidiness one:
# a page dump can carry a URL, a hostname or a header that the guidance at the top of AGENTS.md
# says does not belong in a public repo.
#
# `.claude/worktrees/` and NOT `.claude/`: three paths under it are tracked on purpose - the
# session-start hook, `settings.json` and the skills symlink - and ignoring the parent would hide
# them from `git status` for everyone who edits one. Narrow the pattern to the scratch.
#
# Both were caught by `cargo xtask max-lines` walking into them rather than by anyone noticing,
# which is the useful part: the gate that fails on a 4000-line page dump is the only thing that
# was looking. The worktree half of that walk is fixed separately in the gate itself; ignoring
# the directories is the half that keeps them out of a commit.
/.playwright-mcp/
/.claude/worktrees/
